CloseThreadpoolIo and the I/O completion thread must not both free a threadpool
I/O object.

TpReleaseIoCompletion() set shutting_down and, when pending_count and
skipped_count were both zero, called tp_ioqueue_unlock(). The completion
thread does the same drop when it dequeues a packet, sees shutting_down, and
finds both counts already zero. CancelThreadpoolIo() reaches that state: it
decrements pending_count while the completion is still queued, and it used to
wrap the count if the packet had already been taken. The second side aborted
in assert(ioqueue.objcount) at threadpool.c:2102, or freed the object twice.

Scam With Your Friends (Unity 6000.3, Mono) hits this on every Kolkata OS
recording teardown. The recorder disposes its audio named pipe from
KolkataRecordingAudioSession.WriteAudio, Mono calls CloseThreadpoolIo, and
ntdll aborts. Three crashes on 2026-10-18 (13:04, 13:12, 13:26 UTC) on engine
x64-crossover26.3-r4, macOS 27, Apple Silicon. The faulting instruction is
RtlRaiseStatus from _assert. A later crash the same day was in d3d11 and is
not this bug.

Destruction is now claimed once, with ioqueue.cs taken before pool->cs, the
same order the completion thread already uses. The winner unlists the object
before freeing it, so a packet that is still queued afterwards does not
touch the memory. A completion that is still expected keeps the object alive
and still runs its callback; TpWaitForIoCompletion(..., TRUE) still only
counts those completions as skipped. TpCancelAsyncIoOperation() does not
decrement pending_count below zero.

Verified 2026-10-18 on an Apple Silicon Mac, macOS 27, against this ntdll
running under a copy of engine x64-crossover26.3-r4-recording. A small
program created a named pipe, associated a threadpool I/O object, and
checked four cases: release with nothing pending frees the object
immediately; release while a cancelled wait still expects a completion
keeps it until that packet arrives and does not run the callback; release
while a start is outstanding runs the callback once and then frees the
object; forty cancels with the completion still queued, and forty more
where cancel races a queued completion, do not abort. The previous
marker-only build of this patch failed the immediate-free check. Not yet
run inside the game. Upstream still has the racing path in Wine 11 and in
master; not sent.

